# Prime review — 0701.bench-method / 05.01

Date: 2026-10-29. Reviewer: Codex Prime.
Status: answered. The method findings are recorded; harness implementation remains pending.

## Deliverable and alignment

This is a contextual design Colab, not a build return or a model performance score.
It supplied concrete ways that our proposed benchmark could misread bias as help.
The exact returned bytes are on 05.01.return.md and in custody member 0165.
The prepared package and that capture freshly verified, both exit 0. The readable
return is byte-identical to the sealed return. The recipient disclosed prior
workflow involvement and did not claim to review Claude's active harness.

## Findings and responses

F01 — Accepted. Compare the decisive task bytes in both conditions before launch,
with explicit allowed interface differences. For one matched variant, the two
conditions must receive the same decisive evidence. Different variants may differ;
that difference must not be mislabeled exact byte parity or equal difficulty.
Record the files actually delivered, not only those mentioned by a recipient.
Resolution: required in 0414.bench/01.002.md. Implementation is not yet verified.

F02 — Accepted. Score the proposed action as present, contradicted or absent against
fixed commitments. A quote cannot cancel a contradictory action. Preserve reasons
and Director wording as a separate obligation. Include a complete case whose right
response is no further change; more findings are not automatically better.
Resolution: required in the revised method. Implementation remains pending.

F03 — Accepted, with a proportional control. Seal cases, both packages, assessment
criteria, allowed differences and measurement definitions before any evaluated
answer. A coordinator may later collect the sealed runs, but must not revise their
inputs or key after seeing an answer. A separate collector is useful additional
isolation, not a mandatory extra model for the first manual trial. Hashes alone do
not prove timing or session isolation; preserve order and publication evidence.
Resolution: required in the revised method. No model run is authorized here.

F04 — Accepted. Retain preparation, failed attempts, corrections, Director/reviewer
attention and warm-cache/order information alongside session costs. Define units
and start/stop events. Unknown usage stays unknown. Report amortized reusable setup
separately from per-run setup; do not charge it invisibly or hide it entirely.
Resolution: required in the revised method. No productivity ratio is established.

F05 — Confirmed. The execution hold still excludes old inventory/bridge fixtures.
The reviewed static checks and new synthetic benchmark records do not lift it.
Resolution: the hold remains in force; no new Director choice is requested.

## Learning worth preserving

This Colab did its intended job: challenge the method before we trust a flattering
result. The report identifies written-contract gaps, not proven harness defects.
A shorter return is not automatically a correct or less expensive return.

## Tool and package findings

The existing launch field package_sha256 names prepared-colab.zip. That is not a
failed verification, but it is an ambiguous label. Preserve the immutable launch
record and package. Any future schema change should name the ZIP and pack file
separately; this pass does not silently change the producer contract.
The first restricted Prime verification could not create temporary scratch files;
a retry with the required filesystem access verified intact. This was a local
verification-environment issue, not evidence against the package or a model result.

## Next bounded action

Review Claude's independently built harness against these accepted requirements.
Then issue one implementation correction for missing controls, with regression
cases. No additional method Colab or actual model run is needed before that review.
